Let the total weight of the five initial weights be \( T \). Since the average of these five weights is 13 grams, we can express this as: \[
\frac{T}{5} = 13
\] From this, we can solve for \( T \): \[
T = 13 \times 5 = 65 \text{ grams}
\] When a new weight of 7 grams is added, the total weight becomes: \[
T_{\text{new}} = 65 + 7 = 72 \text{ grams}
\] The average of the six weights is then: \[
\frac{T_{\text{new}}}{6} = \frac{72}{6} = 12 \text{ grams}
\] </think> <think>The average of six weights is \(\boxed{12}\) grams. </think>

